# Component files and folders

- One React component per file.
- Each component lives in a same-named folder with a same-named PascalCase file:
  `UserGreeting/UserGreeting.tsx`.
- If component B is used only by component A, put B under
  `A/components/B/B.tsx`.
- Do not put multiple components in the same file.
- Non-component helpers used only by that component may stay in the same file without export.
- After adding a shadcn component via CLI, move it into this structure (folder + PascalCase file + default export).

```text
Button/
  Button.tsx

UserGreeting/
  UserGreeting.tsx
  components/
    UserName/
      UserName.tsx
```

```tsx
// BAD
components/ui/button.tsx      // kebab-case, flat ui path
app/UserGreeting.tsx          // file without folder
app/UserName.tsx              // sibling of parent, not nested

// GOOD
components/Button/Button.tsx
app/UserGreeting/UserGreeting.tsx
app/UserGreeting/components/UserName/UserName.tsx
```
